pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive-direction companion to `pol_multiply_zero_forged_cardinality`:
% multiplying by 0 is a sound cutting-planes step and must keep working. It
% yields the empty `0 >= 0`, so `pol 1 0 * 2 +` must derive constraint 2
% unchanged -- the true, weaker result that the forgery replaced with
% `1 x1 1 x2 >= 2`. The fix must not be satisfiable by rejecting `0 *`.
f 3 ;
pol 1 0 * ;
e >= 0 : 4 ;
pol 1 0 * 2 + ;
e 2 x2 >= 2 : 5 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
